      "text": [
        " : سَأَلْتُ أَبَا عَبْدِ اَللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَنْ رَجُلٍ أَوْصَى بِجُزْءٍ مِنْ مَالِهِ فَقَالَ\n\"جُزْءٌ مِنْ عَشَرَةٍ قَالَ اَللَّهُ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ ۝ ثُمَّ اِجْعَلْ عَلىٰ كُلِّ جَبَلٍ مِنْهُنَّ جُزْءاً ۝ وَ كَانَتِ اَلْجِبَالُ عَشَرَةً."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.5476 - It is narrated from Al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Faddal, from Thalabah ibn Maymun, from Muawiyah ibn Ammar, who said:\nI asked Abu Abdullah Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as) about a man who bequeathed a portion of his wealth.\nImam (as) replied: \"A portion is one-tenth.\" Allah (swt), the Almighty, said:\n\"Then place on every mountain a portion (juz') of them\" (Surah Al-Baqarah 2:260), and the mountains were ten."
        ]
      }
    },
